pairwire.dev — static landing + download site
==============================================

Plain HTML5 / CSS (OKLCH custom properties) / vanilla JS.
No build tool, no bundler, no node_modules.

Files
-----
  index.html    Main landing page
  styles.css    All styles (OKLCH tokens, Geist font via Google Fonts)
  download.js   Enhances the download button via GitHub Releases API
  version.json  Update-check contract consumed by Workstream E
  assets/       logo.png (brand mark + favicon)

Download button strategy
------------------------
The <a> button carries a static href:

  https://github.com/Bilaltariq98/pairwire/releases/latest/download/pairwire-macos.dmg

This works with JavaScript disabled.

download.js ENHANCES: on DOMContentLoaded it fetches
  https://api.github.com/repos/Bilaltariq98/pairwire/releases/latest
finds the first .dmg asset, and sets btn.href to its browser_download_url.
It also populates the version label from tag_name.
On any error it fails silently and the static href remains.

IMPORTANT — release.yml requirement
------------------------------------
The release workflow (release.yml) MUST upload the macOS DMG asset under
the stable name "pairwire-macos.dmg". This ensures the no-JS static path
always resolves. The API-enhanced path finds any .dmg regardless of name.

Local development
-----------------
  python3 -m http.server 8000 --directory site
  open http://localhost:8000

Or with just:
  just serve-site
  just check-site

version.json schema
-------------------
Three string fields only. Consumed by crates/app/src/update_check.rs.
  { "version": "x.y.z", "url": "https://...", "notes": "..." }
